'''''Sant Martí del Nord, Tramuntana''''' ({{lang|ca|Sant Martí del Nord}}) is a town in the [[La Taula]] comarca of [[Tramuntana Province]], [[Balboa]]. With a population of 14,420 (2026 estimate), it is the largest settlement in the comarca and serves as its administrative capital. Sant Martí del Nord is located in the far north of the Balboa isthmus, in the highland interior of Tramuntana Province, and is one of the northernmost settlements in the country. The town is situated approximately 60 km southeast of [[Sant Jorge, Tramuntana|Sant Jorge]], the comarca's second-largest settlement.

The [[Sant Martí del Nord Airport]] (IATA: SMN, ICAO: SMIB), the northernmost airport in Balboa, connects the town to the national air network via [[Cecilio Ríos International Airport|Sant Bart]] on the [[Aeroístmus]] essential services route.

== Geography ==

Sant Martí del Nord is situated in the northern highlands of Tramuntana Province, on the western (Shendan) slope of the [[Yalabirga Mountain Range|Yalabirga]] range. The town occupies a highland valley at an elevation of approximately 900 metres above sea level. The surrounding terrain is rugged, with steep ridges and forested slopes rising above the valley floor. The climate is cooler and drier than the coastal lowlands, with a pronounced wet season from May to November. The Shendan-facing slope lies in the rain shadow of the higher Yalabirga peaks to the east, resulting in drier conditions than the Aethiopian side of the range.

The town is located in the far north of the Balboa isthmus, near the watershed divide between the Shendan and Aethiopian drainage basins. The [[Sant Martí del Nord Airport]] is located on the northern edge of the settlement, taking advantage of one of the few areas of relatively flat terrain in the area.

== History ==

The area around Sant Martí del Nord has been inhabited by the [[Birú people|indigenous Birú]] for centuries. The Birú retreated into the northern highlands following the Volisanian conquest of the isthmian coast and maintained communities in relative isolation throughout the colonial period.

The town's name, derived from the Volisanian name for [[St. Martin|Sant Martí]], indicates a colonial-era origin. The "del Nord" (of the North) suffix distinguishes it from other settlements named Sant Martí in the Balboan isthmus, reflecting its position as one of the northernmost Volisanian settlements in the colonial highland network. The settlement served as a minor administrative and agricultural centre for the surrounding highland communities throughout the colonial and republican periods.

The [[Sant Martí del Nord Airport]] was constructed to provide a reliable year-round transport link to the remote highland community, replacing the seasonal road access that had previously been the only connection to the provincial network. The airport is the northernmost in Balboa and operates as an essential services destination under the national air connectivity programme.

== Economy ==

The economy of Sant Martí del Nord is based primarily on agriculture and small-scale mining. The valley floor and surrounding highland slopes support the cultivation of maize, beans, and root vegetables, primarily for local consumption. Small mining operations in the surrounding highlands provide supplementary employment. As the comarca capital, the town also serves as an administrative centre for the La Taula comarca, hosting the municipal offices and public services that serve the surrounding rural communities.

The town has a health clinic, a primary school, and a secondary school. The municipal council provides basic services, though infrastructure remains limited compared to the provincial average. The provincial government has identified the La Taula comarca as a priority area for development assistance under the national rural development programme.

== Indigenous community ==

Sant Martí del Nord is located in proximity to several [[Birú people|Birú]] communities in the northern highlands. The Birú population in the area has raised concerns about land use, environmental impact, and the disruption of cultural sites in connection with development projects. The broader tension between infrastructure development and indigenous land rights in the Tramuntana highlands has been a recurring issue for the comarca's communities.

== Transport ==

{{main|Sant Martí del Nord Airport}}

[[Sant Martí del Nord Airport]] (IATA: SMN, ICAO: SMIB) is a domestic airport located on the northern edge of the town. It is the northernmost airport in Balboa and is served by [[Aeroístmus]], which operates essential services from [[Cecilio Ríos International Airport|Sant Bart]]. The airport handled approximately 40,000 passengers in 2025.

Road connections to Sant Martí del Nord include a regional road linking the town to [[Sant Jorge, Tramuntana|Sant Jorge]] to the northwest and a road south to [[Portblanc]], the provincial capital. The roads are narrow and winding, reflecting the rugged highland terrain, and are frequently affected by landslides during the wet season.

